== dedent | @docstring.txt
  |Parse a configuration file.⏎⏎The file is read line by line; each line is either a comment,⏎a section header or a key-value pair.⏎⏎    Nested examples keep their extra indent.⏎⇥A tab after the margin stays.⏎⏎Returns a dict of dicts.⏎|
== dedent | @mixed.txt
  |  two spaces⏎⇥one tab⏎  ⇥two spaces then a tab⏎⏎  back to two⏎|
== dedent | @notes.md
  |Kāra's ownership model has three tiers: owned values, borrowed references and reference-counted shared values. Most code never needs the third.⏎⏎A long identifier like configuration_loader_with_environment_overrides_and_defaults does not fit on one line, nor does https://docs.example.org/very/long/path/to/a/page.html at all.⏎⏎Distances are written 10¤km and 2¤h; the no-break space keeps each pair together. Café, naïve and façade are words too.⏎⏎Short.⏎|
== dedent |     a⏎      b⏎    c
  |a⏎  b⏎c|
== dedent |   a⏎⇥b
  |  a⏎⇥b|
== dedent | ⏎   ⏎   x⏎   y⏎ 
  |⏎⏎x⏎y⏎|
== dedent |    only⏎   
  |only⏎|
== dedent | 
  ||
== dedent |   ␍⏎  x
  |␍⏎x|
